From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: explorer: a window dragged into a corner snaps to a quarter

Dragging a window's title bar to the middle of the left or right edge
snapped it to that half (0075); into a corner -- within 48 px of it, on
either edge -- it now snaps to that quarter of the work area, with the same
outline first. Win+Up and Win+Down move a snapped half to its top or bottom
quarter and back, and Win+Down on a bottom quarter minimizes, as on Windows
10. A window snapped from one place to another comes back to where it was
before the first snap.

Gate: test/shellkeys-gate.sh (make test-shellkeys).
